From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] lvgl: check signed rectangle bounds before drawing

The D211 T-HEAD GCC 10.2 toolchain miscompiles the short width/height
comparison at -O1: it loads the endpoints unsigned, subtracts them, and
branches without narrowing the difference back to lv_coord_t. A valid
rectangle crossing zero is therefore rejected before the software/GE
backend can clip it. Its children still draw, making card backgrounds
and borders disappear while they pass the left screen edge.

Check endpoint ordering directly in the common rectangle entry point.
This keeps signed coordinates, normal clipping, backend selection and
the existing lv_coord_t ABI intact, including large-coordinate builds.

diff --git a/src/draw/lv_draw_rect.c b/src/draw/lv_draw_rect.c
--- a/src/draw/lv_draw_rect.c
+++ b/src/draw/lv_draw_rect.c
@@ -63,7 +63,10 @@ void lv_draw_rect(lv_draw_ctx_t * draw_ctx, const lv_draw_rect_dsc_t * dsc, const lv
 {
-    if(lv_area_get_height(coords) < 1 || lv_area_get_width(coords) < 1) return;
+    /* Test the signed bounds directly. The D211 T-HEAD GCC 10.2 toolchain
+     * miscompiles the narrowed width/height comparison at -O1 when an area
+     * crosses zero, skipping a visible rectangle before clipping it. */
+    if(coords->x1 > coords->x2 || coords->y1 > coords->y2) return;
 
     draw_ctx->draw_rect(draw_ctx, dsc, coords);
 
     LV_ASSERT_MEM_INTEGRITY();
 }
